# ==============================================================================
# Lychee Exception Register
# ==============================================================================
#
# Each entry may be a URL, glob, or regular expression.
# Add exclusions only for destinations that are intentionally unavailable to
# automated clients, and document why the exception exists.

# LinkedIn commonly rejects automated link-checking clients.
^https://(www\.)?linkedin\.com/

# Salesforce developer docs return 403 for automated clients.
^https://developer\.salesforce\.com/

# npmjs.com/support returns 403 for automated clients.
^https://www\.npmjs\.com/support

# The CoffeeLint MegaLinter descriptor was removed; the reference URL is a
# retained comment pointing to the original descriptor location.
^https://megalinter\.io/latest/descriptors/coffee_coffee_lint/

# egohygiene.io and egohygiene.github.io are placeholder domains and GitHub
# Pages that are not yet deployed.
^https?://egohygiene\.io/
^https?://egohygiene\.github\.io/

# URLs containing unexpanded shell-variable references (e.g. ${VAR}) are
# template strings in scripts, not real hyperlinks.
\$\{[^}]+\}

# https://github/ (without a hostname path) is an invalid URL that lychee may
# extract from malformed text; it is not a resolvable endpoint.
^https://github/$
